# Predictive Modeler report

## Task

Detect counterfeit Swiss banknotes from physical measurements. Predict binary target y, with 1 meaning counterfeit and 0 genuine, at prediction time using a subset of the eligible raw measurement columns length, left, right, bottom, top, and diagonal. Use a stratified random split and evaluation seed 42 for randomized splitting and fitting. The deployed model may require no more than three raw measurement columns. Optimize F1 for positive class 1.

## Outcome

Status: succeeded. Stop reason: diminishing_returns.

## Agent rationale

All three trial slots were used and every successful candidate was evaluated. The compact linear model using length, left, and diagonal achieved the best feasible mean cross-validated positive-class F1 (0.981427), exceeding the ExtraTrees alternative (0.975723) and baseline (0.666667); further search is unavailable under the trial budget.

## Evaluation

```json
