# Predictive Modeler report

## Task

Forecast the next 24 hourly values for every ERCOT regional series, using unique_id as the series identifier and timestamp as the hourly time column. Use only each series' historical target observations and calendar information (no external predictors), evaluate chronologically on complete 24-step horizons without reading future values, weight series and evaluation origins equally, and use seed 42 for randomized splitting and fitting where applicable.

## Outcome

Status: succeeded. Stop reason: budget_exhausted.

## Agent rationale

Three candidates were evaluated chronologically on complete 24-step horizons. The 24-hour seasonal-naive model is the measured winner with mean CV MAE 423.4228298611111, improving substantially over persistence (1112.9550173611112) and outperforming the lagged extra-trees model (450.17093130776794); the trial budget is exhausted.

